- content_for :body_class, "trip-what-to-expect-page"
= render "shared/public_header"
%main.public-main
  %section.panel.trip-what-to-expect-panel
    .panel-header
      %div
        %h1 What to expect on a Cragmont trip
        %p.muted A quick topo for your first outing with the club.
    %section.trip-expectation-copy
      %h2 Before the trip
      %p Cragmont trips are community camping and climbing weekends. Participants should expect shared planning, clear communication from the trip team, and a little flexibility as weather, campsite logistics, and climbing objectives come into focus.
      %h2 At camp
      %p You will check in with the trip crew, get oriented to campsite expectations, and coordinate meals, gear, and timing with the group. Bring what you need to be comfortable outside and ready to lend a hand around camp.
      %h2 At the crag
      %p Climbing plans depend on experience levels, route conditions, and the group. Come ready to communicate, support your partners, and keep the stoke high while everyone moves safely.
